\ S6d probe Q — the ROOTLESS one-sided join asymmetry: the exact shape the
\ proposed union admits (frame item 5(a), pinned at the branch join WITHOUT
\ any impl, so today's bytes are the baseline). One if-arm packs the word's
\ seeded slice parameter directly (a parameter slot is `Slot::computed` —
\ deriv-free, so the construction push forwards none); the other arm binds
\ the parameter first, whose naming reborrows it into a deriv with no owned
\ root (the name-read push, src/check/terms.rs:248). The join refuses the
\ asymmetry today with S6d-8.2's exact wording shape; post-union (a rootless
\ one-sided asymmetry carries the deriv) this word checks — build_ok — with
\ no other change.
import: intrinsics * ;
import: core::prelude * ;
import: hosted::show | . | ;

type: Step['T 'Rest]
| Done
| More 'T 'Rest
;

: rootless-asym inline ( Slice[i64] -- Step[i64 Slice[i64]] )
  True
  ~[ 7 swap More ]
  ~[ |x| x 7 swap More ]
  if ;
